sycl: strided SCALE for views

HomeBrain patch on ggml-sycl. Applies on top of 0002.
Upstream tracking: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/32757

Inkling 2's SITU activation scales non-contiguous views of the fused gate/up
output. ggml-sycl only took a contiguous SCALE, so each one became a CPU split
(96 per graph). An element-wise kernel over the view strides keeps them on the
GPU: measured on an Arc Pro B60 with Inkling-2-Mini Q4_K_XL, graph splits went
194 -> 2, decode 17.1 -> 20.9 t/s, prefill 156 -> 192 t/s.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
index 77a9a419b..3b303deb3 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
@@ -2596,6 +2596,27 @@ static void scale_f32_sycl(const float *x, float *dst, const float scale, const
 }
 
 
+// Strided variant for views, e.g. the gate and up halves of a fused gate_up
+// matmul that Inkling 2's SITU activation scales. Without it the op falls back
+// to the CPU, which costs a GPU->CPU->GPU round trip per layer.
+static void scale_f32_nc_sycl(const ggml_tensor * src, ggml_tensor * dst, const float scale, const float bias,
+                              queue_ptr stream) {
+    const int64_t ne0 = src->ne[0], ne1 = src->ne[1], ne2 = src->ne[2];
+    const size_t  s0 = src->nb[0], s1 = src->nb[1], s2 = src->nb[2], s3 = src->nb[3];
+    const size_t  t0 = dst->nb[0], t1 = dst->nb[1], t2 = dst->nb[2], t3 = dst->nb[3];
+    const char *  x = (const char *) src->data;
+    char *        d = (char *) dst->data;
+    stream->parallel_for(sycl::range<1>(ggml_nelements(src)), [=](sycl::id<1> id) {
+        int64_t i = id[0];
+        const int64_t i0 = i % ne0; i /= ne0;
+        const int64_t i1 = i % ne1; i /= ne1;
+        const int64_t i2 = i % ne2;
+        const int64_t i3 = i / ne2;
+        const float v = *(const float *) (x + i0*s0 + i1*s1 + i2*s2 + i3*s3);
+        *(float *) (d + i0*t0 + i1*t1 + i2*t2 + i3*t3) = scale*v + bias;
+    });
+}
+
